New /home/test/neorv32_rot/Makefile orchestrates the cross-repo build:

  tpu-then-rot
    ├── tpu-bitstream      (Quartus + cpf in $TPU_REPO)
    ├── tpu-zeta-verify    (ζ byte-identity gate; skip with ZETA_VERIFY=0)
    ├── tpu-copy           (tpu.rbf → output/tpu.rbf)
    ├── rot-firmware       (sw/stage2_loader/make all → gen_golden.py
    │                       picks up output/tpu.rbf, bakes SHA into
    │                       rot_golden_tpu_bitstream, installs to
    │                       neorv32_imem_image.vhd)
    ├── rot-bitstream      (Quartus + cpf in quartus/ → output/neorv32_demo.rbf
    │                       carries TPU hash in IMEM)
    └── rot-zeta-verify    (ζ byte-identity gate on ROT.rbf)

Env-overridable: TPU_REPO, EP4CE6_REPO, QUARTUS_BIN, XPACK_BIN,
ZETA_VERIFY. Toolchain PATH (xpack-riscv-none-elf + Quartus 21.1)
plumbed via $(PATH_FULL).

End-to-end ex-Quartus test:
  cp /home/test/neorv32_tpu/neorv32_tpu.rbf output/tpu.rbf
  cd sw/stage2_loader && make all
  → rot_golden.h embeds 5e87f3ddd43a3c93... = sha256(neorv32_tpu.rbf) ✓

Plan reference: /home/test/.claude/plans/temporal-booping-raven.md
Phase 5 of 6 (~2h estimate). Quartus invocations in
tpu-bitstream/rot-bitstream not exercised here (no Quartus session
in the test harness); they replicate the canonical commands from
both repos' READMEs.

